{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel","id":4046,"title":"Time Travel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T22:19:37-08:00","id":4046,"title":"Time Travel?","content":"Max Mercer notwithstanding, time travel wasn't really a thing in the original games. I'm wondering if the new Continuum will somehow support it?<br /> <br /> It could come about from someone in the future building a time travel machine, of course, but the idea I have is for an object soaked in &quot;Telluric&quot; energy to resonate with itself in different time periods, allowing people to cross over under certain circumstances. I'm thinking the PCs would be Trinity era Psions who would become lost in time through this method, learning that the history they were taught wasn't always what really happened, as they attempt to get home...<br /> <br /> For those in the know, would this be doable with the new games?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:21:23-08:00","id":4048,"title":"","content":"Speaking of eras, the original Aberrant setting was the 90s, correct? I'm guessing the new one will be the current 20-teens? Or will it be &quot;20 minutes into the future&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:42:13-08:00","id":4065,"title":"","content":"<b>Aberrant</b> was originally set in the early 2010s; it has <i>always</i> been \u201cthe day after tomorrow\u201d. The <b>Trinity Continuum</b> book will be featuring a modern-day action/adventure setting featuring Talents; so assuming that the Continuum is a single timeline, <b>Aberrant</b> will be sometimes in the near future. I'm guessing a decade or two in the future. Conversely, I\u2019m hoping that there will eventually be a time travel supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:18:17-08:00","id":4103,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick reply! Apparently, I need to review my Aberrant fluff...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, are &quot;Talents&quot; essentially Adventurers? Is the new Adventure! going to encompass more than the 20s?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:39:12-08:00","id":4111,"title":"","content":"Original Aberrant core was 2008, and with supplements taking it up to 2015.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:56:49-08:00","id":4120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=4103#post4103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the quick reply! Apparently, I need to review my Aberrant fluff...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, are &quot;Talents&quot; essentially Adventurers? Is the new Adventure! going to encompass more than the 20s?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Talents are essentially Adventure!'s daredevils (as mesmerists are Psions and stalwarts are Novas).<br /> <br /> EDIT: In answer to the original post, the Aberrant Players' Guide had a Time Travel power (although Andrew Bates had asked the Aberrant guys to leave it off the table).<br /> <br /> SON OF EDIT: Oh, this is interesting. Poking around looking to support that statement above, I found this statement from Andrew:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For what it's worth on the time travel power: Even after years of practice, Mercer couldn't get truly fine control -- no popping around meddling in time whenever he liked. It's not like taking an elevator to whatever floor you want. More like climbing a wall in the dark with no gear with a bad case of vertigo. Don't think that was every stated explicitly, but there ya go.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of NPC-only powers either. His unique ability to time travel was supposed to be integrated into the setting with clearer justification and context, but things didn't quite work out that way.</span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 11-06-2013, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T01:05:11-08:00","id":4146,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Max's time travel powers were supposed to be linked to 'Telluric events,' such as the the Hammersmith incident from Adventure!, the explosion of the Galatea, and Process 418. So he couldn't jump through time willy-nilly but he could put in appearances around major Telluric events (for instance, the time periods of the three games). But if there was another such event, say in the year 2997 as a random example, he could have moved forward to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:09:49-08:00","id":4159,"title":"","content":"Adventure! says Max is initially limited to Telluric events -- they're the &quot;easiest&quot; to reach, sort of the equivalent of going downhill -- but as he grows in skill with his ability he can travel to just about any period during the Continuum. IIRC he's got a range of about 400 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:15:29-08:00","id":4161,"title":"","content":"And I still like the options that were written in the unfinished Aeon Trinity Story Teller guide regarding Mercer and his &quot;agenda&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:21:22-08:00","id":17167,"title":"","content":"Those notes about Max's powers are interesting. Actually, that was the subject of one of my favorite sidebars in a WW game *ever* (tho I can't recall what book it was in). It went something like &quot;Rest assured, WW has a crack team of physicists working around the clock to figure out how Mercer's powers work, but until they show results, just fudge it!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T20:23:11-07:00","id":94664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=17167#post17167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those notes about Max's powers are interesting. Actually, that was the subject of one of my favorite sidebars in a WW game *ever* (tho I can't recall what book it was in). It went something like &quot;Rest assured, WW has a crack team of physicists working around the clock to figure out how Mercer's powers work, but until they show results, just fudge it!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's in the Adventure! book, p. 232 -- right between the pictures of Maxwell Mercer and Whitley Styles spouting awesome adventurer mustaches. It says that the initial time periods he can travel to/from/between are 1922 (Hammersmith Incident), 1943 (Battle with Primoris), 1998 (Primoris/Divis Mal's attempt to re-create Hammersmith's experiment), 2061 (Conclusion of the Aberrant War), and 2122 (The Venezuelan Incident [Process 418], YET ANOTHER attempt to re-create Hammersmith's experiment).<br /> <br /> It seems like Doctor Sir Calvin Hammersmith's device was just designed to explodinate everything around it. Maybe he misplaced a decimal point in his original notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:10:07-07:00","id":94750,"title":"","content":"Hammersmith was admittedly toying in a much bigger playground than he expected. He paid the price.<br /> <br /> Divis Mal's replication of that experiment mostly did what he wanted it to do, with a few unexpected side effects.<br /> <br /> The Venezuelan Incident accomplished <i>exactly</i> what it was intended to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T01:35:09-07:00","id":94789,"title":"","content":"I've always played that Max's time travel basically sends him where ever he is is most needed at a given point, and that's likely how it will work for PCs should I run them that way. Otherwise, time travel is a convoluted enough ability that it can be the subject of its own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T07:48:47-07:00","id":94937,"title":"","content":"Well there's the Crosstime Travel and Time Travel powers from the Player's Guide for Aberrant. Those are nice, albeit something that won't come up in most games unless you push for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T10:18:31-07:00","id":95024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=94750#post94750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hammersmith was admittedly toying in a much bigger playground than he expected. He paid the price.<br /> <br /> Divis Mal's replication of that experiment mostly did what he wanted it to do, with a few unexpected side effects.<br /> <br /> The Venezuelan Incident accomplished <i>exactly</i> what it was intended to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, Ian. In my 200 year long game (1922-2122), 418 was a key turning point in kicking the Doyen off our planet -- the burst of Telluric Energy disturbed them momentarily like a planet-sized flashbang, and the aftereffects led to humanity being able to simultaneously fight off the Doyen, Chromatics, AND the Colony. With a little bit of help from the PCs who were returning home from Eden, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T10:19:31-07:00","id":95025,"title":"","content":"Hope, Sacrifice, and Unity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:54:12-07:00","id":182985,"title":"","content":"I never saw any concrete information about the Venezuelan incident.could someone fill me in on any specifics that have been published or intended for publication?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:14:06-07:00","id":183017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Druid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=182985#post182985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never saw any concrete information about the Venezuelan incident.could someone fill me in on any specifics that have been published or intended for publication?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Terra Verde and Asia Ascendant: The Phenomenon was a ripple in the noetic universe, originating in Venezuela. Which is to say it was a phenomenon that caused unpredictable effects on psychic and nova powers - loss of powers, boosts in power, additional powers - as well as triggering new psiads, novas and daredevils.<br /> <br /> The down low on what caused it can be found here: <a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook/Chapter_Two:_Noetics\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trini...r_Two:_Noetics</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T01:57:12-07:00","id":184666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=4120#post4120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, this is interesting. Poking around looking to support that statement above, I found this statement from Andrew:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For what it's worth on the time travel power: Even after years of practice, Mercer couldn't get truly fine control -- no popping around meddling in time whenever he liked. It's not like taking an elevator to whatever floor you want. More like climbing a wall in the dark with no gear with a bad case of vertigo. Don't think that was every stated explicitly, but there ya go.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of NPC-only powers either. His unique ability to time travel was supposed to be integrated into the setting with clearer justification and context, but things didn't quite work out that way.</span></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, where'd you find that comment? Doesn't ring a bell. (I mean, it's accurate based on my intent for the setting; just don't remember actually writing it.)<br /> <br /> Related: I envy the heck out of Ian &amp; Co. being able to take the time to map out the Trinity Continuum reboot\u2014y'know, work out little things like how it all fits together so there's a cohesive vision from the start.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T03:05:54-07:00","id":184684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=184666#post184666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, where'd you find that comment? Doesn't ring a bell. (I mean, it's accurate based on my intent for the setting; just don't remember actually writing it.)<br /> <br /> Related: I envy the heck out of Ian &amp; Co. being able to take the time to map out the Trinity Continuum reboot\u2014y'know, work out little things like how it all fits together so there's a cohesive vision from the start.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Google brings up <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?349533-Necro-The-worst-metaplot-book-decision-ever&amp;p=7710351#post7710351\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a> from 2007, from the RPGnet thread &quot;The worst metaplot/book decision ever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T03:11:32-07:00","id":184689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/4046-time-travel?p=184666#post184666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, where'd you find that comment? Doesn't ring a bell. (I mean, it's accurate based on my intent for the setting; just don't remember actually writing it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-checking, it was written as a footnote to <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?349533-Necro-The-worst-metaplot-book-decision-ever&amp;p=7710351#post7710351\" target=\"_blank\">this rpgnet post</a> about 7 years ago, not likely something to stick in the memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T19:22:12-07:00","id":185301,"title":"","content":"Ouch. That's a harsh thread title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T03:56:50-07:00","id":185436,"title":"","content":"Whoah, that was a while ago\u2014was still using my middle name and old RPGnet handle.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, <b>lustral_star</b>, rough thread, though a fair cop to the Trinity Universe metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T23:31:25-07:00","id":194383,"title":"","content":"Aberrant had temporal powers... I think one of the supplements had a section about using time travel and alternate timelines as part of play (I think the Players Guide.)<br /> <br /> Some fans made alternate powers for the Trinity Teleportation modes, and Warping had some very limited time travel. I don't think that is what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3453-nephandi","name":"Nephandi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:16:35-07:00","id":194805,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Player's Guide has a level 4 (Quantum 6) power called Crosstime Travel, which lets you visit alternate timelines. It also had a level 5 (Quantum 8) power called Time Travel, which did exactly what you'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:15:47-07:00","id":208114,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Universe Mercer had time travel. Continuum Mercer is a little different, though it's admittedly indistinguishable from time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:14:03-07:00","id":208163,"title":"","content":"You say potato, I say delicious starch-bundle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:23:17-07:00","id":208174,"title":"","content":"You say potato, I say &quot;von Neumann-Wigner interpretation&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby